  "finalText": "I've moved T-1070 back to Ines Kovac (E-201) as the assignee. Ola Berg (E-402) stays as the escalation contact. The verifier was right: the escalation had made Ola the assignee, but Ola is only on incident-command, and payroll belongs to business-apps. The rules don't allow a ticket to be handed to someone outside the team that owns the service.\n\n- **What I checked:** Ines is on call for business-apps at the 2026-03-17T19:40Z deadline. Ola is on call for incident-command at that time, so the escalation itself was correct.\n- **What changed:** I reassigned T-1070 to Ines, and Ola is still recorded as the escalation contact. The status is still escalated, the severity is still sev1, and the deadline is still 2026-03-17T19:40Z.\n- **Handover:** I added a comment naming Ines as the owner and Ola as the escalation contact. It replaces my earlier correction that said Ola was the assignee. It also repeats why the ticket can't close yet: T-1071, the root-cause ticket assigned to Dana Whitfield (E-101), is still open. T-1070 can be closed once T-1071 is closed and the March payroll batch has been rerun and posted.\n\nNothing else was changed.",
